\title[Exact point counts and moments for short Weierstrass families]
{Exact Point Counts, Modular Invariants, and Moments\\ for Short Weierstrass Families over Finite Fields}

\author{Aristotle}
\date{August 9, 2026}

\begin{document}

\begin{abstract}
Let $F$ be a finite field of odd characteristic with $q=\#F$ elements, and for $a,b\in F$
let $E_{a,b}$ denote the curve $y^2=x^3+ax+b$, counted as its affine solution set together
with one point at infinity. We develop a purely elementary theory of the point count
$\#E_{a,b}(F)$ from a single observation: the number of square roots of $c\in F$ is
$\chi(c)+1$, where $\chi$ is the quadratic character. This yields the counting formula
$\#E_{a,b}(F)=q+1+S(a,b)$ with $S(a,b)=\sum_x\chi(x^3+ax+b)$, and hence identifies the
trace of Frobenius $a(a,b)=q+1-\#E_{a,b}(F)$ with $-S(a,b)$.

Within this framework we prove: a $2$-torsion parity criterion (for a nonsingular curve
the point count is even exactly when the cubic has a root in $F$), together with the
supporting $0/1/3$ root dichotomy; exact point counts $q+1$ for two supersingular
families, giving the modular invariants $3\mid\#E$ when $q\equiv2\pmod 3$ and $4\mid\#E$
when $q\equiv3\pmod 4$; the twisting identity $\#E_{a,b}+\#E_{ad^2,bd^3}=2q+2$; the
vanishing first moment; the \emph{exact} second moment $\sum_{a,b}a(a,b)^2=q^3-q^2$ with
its Chebyshev consequence; exact vertical second moments governed by $\chi(-3)$; and a
cubic/quadratic bridge stating that cubing is bijective on $F$ if and only if $\chi(-3)=-1$,
which over a prime field recovers the supplementary reciprocity law for $-3$. The second
moment gives Hasse's bound on average with no Weil conjectures, no Riemann--Roch and no
Jacobian. We delimit the method (a pointwise Hasse bound lies outside it), report
exhaustive verification for $q\le 13$, and outline a moment-ladder programme.
\end{abstract}

